// CROWN — an install's mask stays on its own body: `g2` absorbs E around
// `f(1)` and calls `k(1)` outside the install; `k` performs E, the caller
// declares `!E`. Expect E_EffectMismatch.
//
// Refuses through the pinned boot. The guard on masks: a mask taught onto
// a cell with other sources would cover `k`'s E too.
effect E { op() -> Int }
handler absorb { op() => resume(5) }
fn g2(f, k) = (f(1) ~> absorb) + k(1)
fn clean() with !E = g2({ x => x }, { y => op() + y })
fn main() = 0
